              "ImageDescription": {
                "value": "<p>Found north of Rome\nCollection Gans 1920\nObjects made out of gold, silver, bronze, precious stones, amber, bone and glass.\nEarly 1st Century AD.\n</p>\nThis unusually rich grave furnishing belonged to the grave of a young woman who died before her wedding and which can be dated on the basis of the \"Charon's obol\", a coin of Emperor Tiberius minted in AD 15/16. A wooden box (parts of the lock preserved) contained gold jewellery and an engagement ring with a faceted aquamarine. Further burial objects include: a silver miniature tableware set with beakers, amphorae, bowls, platters, ladle, candelabra and oil lamps, table and stool. Three silver hand mirrors, little containers, flasks and bowls made out of quartz, agate and alabaster as well as little rods made out of bone served the purpose of female cosmetics. Teo bronze ink wells, one ivory writing tablet, a little bone box as well as 70 glass gem stones, a cicada, a shell, a quartz icosahedron and an amber walnut are evidence of the family's wealth.",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "DateTimeOriginal": {
                "value": "2023-02-03 13:48",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "Credit": {
                "value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/photos/mumblerjamie/52670852116/\">Burial Objects from the Grave of a Young Woman - Altes Museum, Berlin</a>",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
              "Artist": {
                "value": "<a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.flickr.com/people/184393744@N06\">Jamie Heath</a> from United Kingdom",
                "source": "commons-desc-page"
              },
